 "caveats": [
  "A booking index of 1.0 means as many yellow cards as the model expects from the fouls recorded and the pre-match situation. It is not a measure of fairness and is never read that way here.",
  "Fouls and cards are as recorded by the source feed. What counts as a foul is not the same in every league, which is why every expectation is fitted within the league.",
  "Intervals are exact Poisson intervals on the count of yellow cards. Early in a season they are wide enough to admit almost anything, and that is the point of showing them.",
  "Percentiles say where a club sits among clubs measured the same way. Nothing here is a ranking, and a sorted list drawn from this file would be one.",
  "The situation multiplier needs odds. A match without them is priced at the era expectation alone.",
  "Completed seasons use their own league-season fit. The season in progress uses the league's pooled fit on completed seasons since 2017-18, frozen, so four matches cannot set their own baseline."
 ],
